ies the Old Post Office/City Hall at 258 Main Street and says it was saved from demolition and adaptively reused as Oneonta’s City Hall.","source_url":"https://oneontahistory.org/events-programs/walking-tours/main-street-walking-tour/","source_title":"Main Street Walking Tour","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View the exterior from Main Street; City Hall access depends on municipal operations.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"riverside-cemetery","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Riverside Cemetery","title":"Pause at Riverside Cemetery","subtitle":"Main Street corridor — 296 Main Street","notes":"Approach respectfully behind First Presbyterian Church and use the tour context to understand why this is Oneonta’s most historic cemetery.","short_summary":"A historic cemetery behind First Presbyterian Church.","evidence_claim":"The walking tour identifies Riverside Cemetery at 296 Main Street as Oneonta’s most historic cemetery and dates the land deed for church, parsonage, and cemetery to 1805.","source_url":"https://oneontahistory.org/events-programs/walking-tours/main-street-walking-tour/","source_title":"Main Street Walking Tour","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use respectful cemetery etiquette and follow any posted access guidance.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"fairchild-mansion-masonic-lodge","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Fairchild Mansion/Masonic Lodge","title":"Look for the Fairchild Mansion’s style","subtitle":"Main Street corridor — 322 Main Street","notes":"View this landmark from the sidewalk and compare its Italianate origins with the Queen Anne remodeling documented on the walking tour.","short_summary":"An 1867 mansion later remodeled in the Queen Anne style.","evidence_claim":"The walking tour identifies Fairchild Mansion/Masonic Lodge at 322 Main Street, built in 1867 and remodeled in 1891 in the Queen Anne style.","source_url":"https://oneontahistory.org/events-programs/walking-tours/main-street-walking-tour/","source_title":"Main Street Walking Tour","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View the exterior from Main Street; do not assume public interior access.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ford-block","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Ford Block","title":"See the saved Ford Block","subtitle":"Main Street corridor — 192–202 Main Street","notes":"Walk this block and use the tour’s account of the 1881 fire and later preservation to add context to the streetscape.","short_summary":"A Main Street commercial block saved after a proposed urban-renewal demolition.","evidence_claim":"The walking tour identifies Ford Block at 192–202 Main Street and states that it was built after an 1881 fire and later saved from planned demolition.","source_url":"https://oneontahistory.org/events-programs/walking-tours/main-street-walking-tour/","source_title":"Main Street Walking Tour","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View the block from the Main Street public corridor.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"clinton-plaza","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Clinton Plaza","title":"Locate the Clinton-Sullivan monument","subtitle":"Main Street corridor — Clinton Plaza","notes":"Use the remaining strip of Brown Park at Clinton Plaza to find the monument to the 1779 Clinton-Sullivan expedition.","short_summary":"A Main Street plaza retaining a small remnant of Brown Park and its monument.","evidence_claim":"The walking tour states that Clinton Plaza retains a strip of the former Brown Park around a monument to the 1779 Clinton-Sullivan expedition.","source_url":"https://oneontahistory.org/events-programs/walking-tours/main-street-walking-tour/","source_title":"Main Street Walking Tour","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use public walkways and observe any posted plaza guidance.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
